{"type":"npc","name":"Eldritch Tyrant","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":400,"temp":0,"max":400,"details":""},"ac":{"value":35,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":50,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":50}],"details":""},"weaknesses":[{"type":"mental","value":10,"exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["aklo"],"details":"Can't speak"},"level":{"value":15},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Eldritch tyrants form when an intelligent aberrant symbiote binds to a tyrannosaurus rex, forming a new apex predator that stands far above the original tyrannosaurus rex on the food chain. Eldritch tyrants aren't usually actively evil, but they're quite destructive, and they have extreme difficulty comprehending the idea that any language other than Aklo is actually a language, rather than a more rudimentary form of communication like the squawks of birds. Someone who can communicate with a typical eldritch tyrant in Aklo has a decent chance to convince it to eat something else instead of a sapient creature, in exchange for acting with the proper deference towards it and perhaps performing tasks on its behalf. However, someone who attempts this strategy on a chaotic evil eldritch tyrant, or one in an especially foul or hungry mood, will quickly realize the result is not always so positive.</p><h2>Mind Over Monster</h2><p>The symbiote psychic sensitivity, the cracks between the symbiote and the tyrannosaurus, and the tyrannosaurus's relatively undeveloped mind without the symbiote's help make an eldritch tyrant vulnerable to the same sorts of psychic energies that it uses to attack others. However, this matter is something of a sore spot for most eldritch tyrants, so there's little chance of engaging in a diplomatic approach after exploiting an eldritch tyrant's weakness to mental effects, or even mentioning it in conversation.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 810/1,850/3,400 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing), armor (medium, heavy), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Intimidation, Occultism, Stealth)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> body, bane, constitution, elongating, energy resistant (vitality), mind, mind shield, music, sensory (darkvision), strength, wild, winged</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"RFC Community","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":9},"dex":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":8},"int":{"mod":4},"wis":{"mod":3},"cha":{"mod":3}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":24,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"thoughtsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":120}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":29,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":24,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":26,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":24},"athletics":{"base":32},"intimidation":{"base":28},"occultism":{"base":25},"stealth":{"base":24}},"traits":{"value":["aberration"],"rarity":"common","size":{"value":"grg"}}},"_id":"4BQjFfinxOGmjWWv","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/eldritch-tyrant.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Eldritch Tyrant","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":4,"height":4,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/eldritch-tyrant.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/subjects/eldritch-tyrant.webp"}},"flags":{"sf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"randomImg":false,"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null},"items":[{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/OneAction.webp","name":"Constrict","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"actions":{"value":1},"category":"offensive","description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The eldritch tyrant has a creature @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.conditions.Item.kWc1fhmv9LBiTuei]{Grabbed} in its mouth tentacle</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The eldritch tyrant constricts the grabbed creature, crushing both its body and mind. The creature takes @Damage[(3d12+4)[bludgeoning]] damage and @Damage[2d6[mental]] damage, with a basic Fortitude save. On a failure, the creature is also @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.conditions.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 1} for 1 minute, and on a critical failure, they're @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.conditions.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 2} for 1 minute instead.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Monster Core","authors":""},"rules":[],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"slug":"constrict","_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":null},"deathNote":false},"type":"action","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.sf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.g26YiEIfSHCpLocV","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"gXuUkHp7XpgDjEgR"},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/OneAction.webp","name":"Swallow Whole","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"actions":{"value":1},"category":"offensive","description":{"value":"<p>Huge, @Damage[3d12[bludgeoning],2d6[mental]], Rupture 39</p><hr /><p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.SwallowWhole]</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Monster Core","authors":""},"rules":[],"traits":{"value":["attack"],"otherTags":[]},"slug":"swallow-whole","_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":null},"deathNote":false},"type":"action","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.sf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.uJSseLa57HZYSMUu","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"4SoTEluluDxUYgm6"},{"type":"action","name":"Grabbing Pull","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The eldritch tyrant's last action was a successful mouth tentacle Strike</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The eldritch tyrant pulls its victim in closer and then grabs it in place. The eldritch tyrant can move the creature it hit with its mouth tentacle towards it by an amount of its choosing. Then it Grabs the creature with its mouth tentacle. It can transfer the creature to be @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.conditions.Item.kWc1fhmv9LBiTuei]{Grabbed} by its jaws instead as a free action, depending on whether it is planning to use Constrict or Swallow Whole next.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":1},"category":"offensiv